    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This abstract describes a study that investigated the reliability and validity of the Body Appreciation Scale (BAS) in 228 Black college women. The study supported the construct validity of the measure and found a moderate, positive association between ethnic identity and body appreciation. Western beauty ideal internalization was found to mediate the relationship between ethnic identity and eating, weight, and shape concerns.",
